      "side": 1,
      "message": "No actually there is a path from [`Settings`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/Android.bp;l\u003d116;drc\u003dc9292dc7927875db35eb02be000a08d7b58bd457) -static_libs-\u003e [`Settings_core`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/apps/Settings/Android.bp;l\u003d52;drc\u003dc9292dc7927875db35eb02be000a08d7b58bd457) -defaults-\u003e [`SettingsLibsDefaults`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/packages/SettingsLib/Android.bp;l\u003d84;drc\u003dafb021d75e6877cced751ccfa42c4be63dcd1708) -static_libs-\u003e [`androidx.mediarouter_mediarouter-nodeps`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/packages/SettingsLib/Android.bp;l\u003d21;drc\u003dafb021d75e6877cced751ccfa42c4be63dcd1708).\n\nAfaict, I\u0027m not seeing a code path that propagates `static_libs` Java code up the dependency chain. It looks like `static_libs` deps have their assets merged and propagated to rdeps. They are [added as implicits](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/java/aapt2.go;l\u003d238;drc\u003d8fe50b072371b0d7c26325e535cf9df0e79e3797) to the link command, and then they get this [`--auto-add-overlay` flag](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/java/aar.go;l\u003d479;drc\u003d8fe50b072371b0d7c26325e535cf9df0e79e3797). But `AARImport` doesn\u0027t call `java.Module.compile`, so it doesn\u0027t do the `TransformJarToJars` for `static_libs` like the other java modules do.",
